  cpp_include_err_missing.pcpp - C++ integration compliance: a missing header

  An #include of a header that does not exist is clang's fatal error
  (ZB0016 "file not found"), reported at the .pcpp line of the #include
  (BNF.md sec 10, DESIGN.md sec 5). The build never ends on only "Build
  failed with exit code 1". This file is built, never run.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\cpp_include_err_missing.pcpp
    pcpp res\tests\cpp_include_err_missing.pcpp -t x86_64-linux-gnu
  The marked line reports that code; nothing else is reported.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe cpp_include_err_missing;

#include <abcde> // ERROR ZB0016@10: 'abcde' file not found

begin
  println("unreachable");
end.
